            <ArticleTitle>Pregabalin (Pfizer).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>82-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pregabalin is a gamma-aminobutyric acid analog that is under development by Pfizer for the potential treatment of central nervous system disorders, including epilepsy, neuropathic pain, fibromyalgia and generalized anxiety disorder. By April 2003, Pfizer had filed for approval of pregabalin in Europe for neuropathic pain and as an adjunctive therapy for epilepsy, and in October 2003 an NDA was filed for these indications and generalized anxiety disorder. At this time, phase III trials in fibromyalgia were ongoing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
